    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0634" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4619: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-08T15:00:00+08:00">March 8, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 8—10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 80, March 7, noon [<hi rendition="#italic">12 p.m.</hi>]. With my British,
                    French and Italian colleagues and our respective commanders in chief we agreed
                    yesterday to pool our information regarding status of military operations and
                    have same forwarded to Geneva through British Minister as Senior Minister. This
                    information will be sent daily to Geneva from now on and serially numbered.
                    Situation report No. 1 was due today. Does the Department desire that I repeat
                    these reports to it?<anchor n="66" xml:id="d571-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d571-f1" n="66" xml:id="d571-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 81, March 8, 5 p.m., the Department requested repetition of
                    reports on the situation referred to.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
